(/--- StaffSync Phase-Wise Implementation Documentation (Page 1 of 7) ---) '
() '
(# StaffSync HRMS   Phase-Wise Implementation Documentation) '
() '
(## Executive Overview) '
(**StaffSync** is an enterprise-grade Human Resource Management System \(HRMS\) built on) '
(   a modern full-stack TypeScript architecture \(React 19, Tailwind CSS v4, Vite, Expr) '
(  ess, and Mongoose/Dual-Engine storage\). This document details each phase of the pro) '
(  ject's inception, design, engineering, integration, and verification.) '
() '
(---) '
() '
(## Table of Phases) '
() '
(| Phase | Phase Name | Primary Objectives & Deliverables | Status |) '
(| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |) '
(| **Phase 1** | Architecture & Data Modeling | Domain entities, TypeScript schemas, A) '
(  PI contracts | Completed |) '
(| **Phase 2** | Dual Storage Engine | MongoDB Atlas cloud driver + resilient in-memor) '
(  y fallback | Completed |) '
(| **Phase 3** | Authentication & RBAC | JWT auth, bcrypt password hashing, 3 role per) '
(  sonas | Completed |) '
(| **Phase 4** | Attendance & Timesheets | Punch clock, shift tracking, attendance aud) '
(  its, manual corrections | Completed |) '
(| **Phase 5** | Multi-Tier Leave Workflow | Leave balances, manager pre-approval, HR ) '
(  final sign-off, cancellation | Completed |) '
(| **Phase 6** | Workforce Directory & Ops | Department units, employee profiles, trai) '
(  ning modules, announcements | Completed |) '
(| **Phase 7** | Audit Trail & Analytics | Immutable compliance logging, CSV reports, ) '
(  department metrics | Completed |) '
(| **Phase 8** | Theme Engine & Dark Mode | CSS variable mapping, dark mode toggle, ze) '
(  ro-contrast defect polish | Completed |) '
(| **Phase 9** | Quality Assurance & Testing | Automated 17-point test suite, edge-cas) '
(  e validation, health checks | Completed |) '
() '
(---) '
() '
(## Phase 1: Architecture & Data Modeling) '
() '
(### 1.1 Objectives) '
(Define the core business entities for modern human resource operations, ensuring stri) '
(  ct separation of concerns, strong TypeScript typings, and normalized relationship m) '
(  odels.) '
() '
ET
endstream
endobj
